# Vulnerability waivers for the image scan in CI (SRS §44.2: High findings need a time-boxed waiver).
# One CVE per line, each with a comment giving the reason, the owner and an expiry date, e.g.:
#   CVE-2026-00000  # not reachable: we never parse X.509 in-process. owner: IT & MIS. expires 2026-12-31
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-10-31  # OpenSSL DTLS retransmission: not reachable, Node.js has no DTLS (TLS over TCP only), and the image's Node.js links its own OpenSSL, not the system libssl. Fixed in Debian 3.5.7-1~deb13u3; drop when the distroless base ships it. owner: IT & MIS. expires 2026-10-31
CVE-2026-75804 exp:2026-10-31  # OpenSSL QUIC denial of service: not reachable, the image's Node.js links its own OpenSSL (3.5.8) and no other binary or addon loads the system libssl. Fixed in Debian 3.5.7-1~deb13u3; drop when the distroless base ships it. owner: IT & MIS. expires 2026-10-31
